    "body": "<!-- issue-cleanup:triage -->\n## Triage analysis\n\n**Clarified summary**\nThe post-draft deckbuilder has no control for designating a drafted companion such as Lutri.\n\n**Expected behavior**\nA legal drafted companion can be moved to the companion slot and validated with the completed main deck.\n\n**Observed behavior**\nThe build-deck screen provides no way to set the companion.\n\n**Reproduction status**\nThe report supplies the complete Cube Draft sequence and named companion.\n\n**Oracle text (verified from `client/public/card-data.json`)**\n### Lutri, the Spellchaser\n> Companion \u2014 Each nonland card in your starting deck has a different name. (If this card is your chosen companion, you may put it into your hand from outside the game for {3} as a sorcery.)\n> Flash\n> When Lutri enters, if you cast it, copy target instant or sorcery spell you control. You may choose new targets for the copy.\n\n**Investigation findings**\nThis is a deckbuilder workflow/state action gap, not a parser defect in Lutri's text.\n\n**Likely scope**\nFrontend draft deck construction and companion-slot actions.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n- A drafted companion can be assigned and removed.\n- Legality is validated against the final deck.\n- The companion persists into game setup.\n\n**Related issues**\nNo exact duplicate was found.",
